            "review_title": "Review at Thien Nam Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jeffrey Lott\nDelaware4 contributions\n0\nEclectic menu and decor\nFeb 2024 • Solo\nI was looking for an aircon restaurant for lunch near the Fine Arts Museum and found this nice Chinese-run place. I ordered duck with black pepper sauce—yum! The menu had a big selection of Vietnamese and Chinese dishes. \n\nMid-afternoon it was not busy so I had a chance to inspect the eclectic decor, including clocks, porcelain figurines, photos of motorcycles and American muscle cars. \n\nWhite tablecloths, refreshing towelettes, and immaculate toilets too!\nRead more\nWritten February 5, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
