            "review_title": "Review at Thien Nam Restaurant",
            "review_text": "sgnhuynh\nSaigon, Vietnam22 contributions\n0\nNostalgic in a very good way, true gem\nJun 2018 • Solo\nIt's easy to overlook and misunderstand this premise. First this is not a new establishment, in fact, when opened during the 1950s, it was one of the earliest restaurant to serve \"Western food\" adapted to the local tastes, the chefs learned from French owned restaurants and started to concoct their own versions of contemporary Western foods such as salads, ox tongues or lamb legs... It was considered an upscale place at that time, but unlike the restricted Continental or Majestic, still accessible to the local population, Vietnamese and Chinese alike. And the amazing thing is most of the dishes remained the same on how they were during that era. You can taste the nostalgia in the \"Assietes Anglaise\", the \"Poussin Farci\" or the \"Poulet Marengo\" , all dishes feature the earliest European-Asian fusion that is impossible now to find at anywhere else. This place is a piece of culinary history of Saigon, enjoy it while it's still there.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 14, 2018",
