            "review_text": "Erick Affrian\nSuzhou, China50 contributions\n0\nAuthentically vietnam / european food\nApr 2017 • Friends\nIt is an old restaurant. Very quaint. You would expect to see many locals in this restaurant. They offered chinese menu, and european menu. \n\nWe didnt get the vietnamese dishes, but the european food is recommended. Good service and prompt. Of course we visited here during late lunch time (around 2pm). There were no one else except us, so we got the personalized service. \n\nWe love the fried rice stuffed in chicken (forgot the name), stuffed crab, and baked clams. The stuffed crab and fried rice are recommended. Look at the pictures. Oh, and the sangria! Love the sangria.\nRead more\nWritten April 2, 2017",
