            "review_text": "Tony K\nSingapore, Singapore1 contribution\n0\nProabaly one of the best fusion of chinese/french\nOct 2016 • Friends\nI have been to this restaurant since 23 years ago and it still remain of of my must visit restaurant whenever i came home. The price is slightly higher than average for vietnamese but it is totally affordable for tourist, a few of their must try dishes in my opinion is \"Com ga roti/roasted chicken rice, spaghetti sot bo ba/minced beef spaghetti, ngheu duc lo pho mai/baked clam with cheese\". Their cuisine is somewhat fusion between chinese and french style.\nRead more\nWritten December 30, 2016",
