            "review_text": "Karno N\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam385 contributions\n0\nCantonese / International comfort foods 😙\nSep 2016 • Friends\nThien Nam is a one of the oldest restaurant establishment since 1968 or even more. So on the outside it looks like a hole in the wall and has a charming characters of the yesteryear on the inside.\n\nService; staffs are well trained and speak Cantonese and some English, but the menu has English subtitles so no worries.\n\nFoods; the foods are ranges from typical to adventurous such as tongue and brain (this reminded me of a typical Mexican Foods menu), but it covers US, Spanish, and Italians dishes with a twist of Cantonese.\n\nThe three of us had Steak & Macaroni, Chicken & Green Peas, Tomato fried rice, Ox tail soup, Roasted quails, Bake clams & cheese, Garlic fried Frog legs, and drinks. \n\nThe above were well proportioned and also fantastically good which reminded me of the many places that I had visited in HongKong and Macau and also in Houston... very homely and comfort 😚\n\nFor dessert, we had Flan and it was so damn delicious 🤓\n\nPrice; with the above we paid 2,040,000.00 VND which is $90 USD. So this wasn't bad at all since there was a doggy bag in-tow when we left the place.\n\nSo, do be adventurous and enjoy the local interpretation of the international comfort foods of the Saigon yesteryear 😘\n\nWell, enjoy, and happy traveling and be safe 🤗\n\nK\n\nPs. While dining I couldn't help myself from thinking that my parents must have been here before during the 60s and early 70s because one of the dish I ordered was my dad's favourite, and what my wife ordered was my mom's favourite. 🤔\nRead more\nWritten September 24, 2016",
